From 93698ae357769147825484fcfbf8c45042607859 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "siheon.ryu" <siheon.ryu@samsung.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:31:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Route all LLM calls through OpenAI-compatible proxy
 (proxy-only mode)

Local patches to run ARTEMIS in a network where direct Google/OpenAI/
Anthropic API hosts are blocked and only an internal LiteLLM proxy is
reachable (OPENAI_BASE_URL). No Gemini/Google API key is required.

- config/artemis.jsonc: switch default, object_detector, hopper,
  flash.step_summarizer and memory.chunking to provider "openai",
  model "gemini/gemini-3.5-flash" (served by the proxy).
- artemis/config/llm.py: lightweight_judge_default() and the no-config
  fallback in _expand_default_into_nodes were hardcoded to provider
  "google"; use "openai" so Pro-mode judges also follow the proxy.
- artemis/agents/flash/summarizer.py, artemis/agents/flash/runner.py,
  artemis/memory/chunking.py: these called get_google_llm() directly,
  bypassing the jsonc model configuration entirely (upstream bug).
  Repointed to get_openai_llm() so the configured provider is honored.

Verified on a Galaxy S26 Ultra via the MCP server: mobile_run_task
completes with all requests going to the proxy and zero calls to
googleapis.com.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
